{
 "ep": 14,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Initialize a PostgreSQL Cluster",
 "phase": "Installation & Administration",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "What does initdb really create?",
   "cap": "What does *initdb* really *create?*"
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode fourteen of the PostgreSQL DBA series. Today: what initdb builds, and what to get right the first time.",
   "cap": "Episode 14: what *initdb* builds, and what to get *right.*",
   "cue": "right"
  },
  {
   "say": "Before PostgreSQL stores anything, you need a database cluster: a set of databases managed by one running server.",
   "cap": "A *cluster:* databases managed by *one* *server.*",
   "cue": "cluster"
  },
  {
   "say": "initdb creates it. First, the data directory and its subdirectories.",
   "cap": "initdb creates the *data* *directory.*",
   "cue": "directory"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then the shared catalog tables, which belong to the whole cluster, not to any one database.",
   "cap": "Then the *shared* *catalog* tables.",
   "cue": "shared"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then three databases: postgres, template one, and template zero.",
   "cap": "Three databases: *postgres,* *template1,* *template0.*",
   "cue": "three"
  },
  {
   "say": "postgres is the default database. The templates are copied by later CREATE DATABASE commands.",
   "cap": "Templates are *copied* by *CREATE DATABASE.*",
   "cue": "copied"
  },
  {
   "say": "Never modify template zero. Objects you add to template one are copied into databases you create later.",
   "cap": "Never modify *template0.* template1 can be *customized.*",
   "cue": "Objects"
  },
  {
   "say": "Let's run it as the postgres user. Dash capital D names the data directory.",
   "cap": "Run as *postgres.* *-D* names the data directory.",
   "cue": "names"
  },
  {
   "say": "Dash capital E sets the encoding, dash dash locale sets the locale, and dash k turns on data checksums.",
   "cap": "*-E* encoding, *--locale,* and *-k* for checksums.",
   "cue": "checksums"
  },
  {
   "say": "initdb confirms the locale, and says data page checksums are enabled. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "Locale *C.UTF-8,* checksums *enabled.*",
   "cue": "enabled"
  },
  {
   "say": "Inside: base, global, pg_wal and the config files. Mode seven hundred, owned by postgres. Output trimmed.",
   "cap": "*base,* *global,* *pg_wal.* Mode *700,* owner postgres.",
   "cue": "seven"
  },
  {
   "say": "Connected to it, SHOW data_checksums returns on, and pg_database lists our three databases.",
   "cap": "*data_checksums* is *on.* Three databases listed.",
   "cue": "lists"
  },
  {
   "say": "Why choose carefully? The docs say the template databases' sort order cannot be changed without dropping and recreating them.",
   "cap": "Template *sort* *order:* drop and *recreate* to change.",
   "cue": "changed"
  },
  {
   "say": "And the WAL segment size can only be set during initialization. The default is sixteen megabytes.",
   "cap": "*WAL* *segment* *size:* set only at initdb. Default *16 MB.*",
   "cue": "only"
  },
  {
   "say": "Checksums: since PostgreSQL eighteen, initdb enables them by default. Our Ubuntu sixteen cluster had them off.",
   "cap": "Checksums: *on* by default since *PostgreSQL 18.*",
   "cue": "eighteen"
  },
  {
   "say": "To change that later, pg_checksums works only on a cluster that is shut down.",
   "cap": "*pg_checksums:* only on an *offline* cluster.",
   "cue": "shut"
  },
  {
   "say": "Common mistake: running initdb as root. It refuses, with the error: cannot be run as root.",
   "cap": "initdb *refuses* to run as *root.*",
   "cue": "refuses"
  },
  {
   "say": "Another: the default trust authentication. initdb warns you. The docs suggest dash capital A scram sha two fifty six, with a password.",
   "cap": "Replace *trust:* use *-A scram-sha-256* and a password.",
   "cue": "warns"
  },
  {
   "say": "On Ubuntu, the package already ran pg_createcluster for you. The docs say: prefer your package's script over running initdb directly.",
   "cap": "Ubuntu ran *pg_createcluster.* Prefer the *package* *script.*",
   "cue": "prefer"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway: a common practice is to fix locale, encoding and checksums in your server build standard.",
   "cap": "Common practice: put these in your *build* *standard.*",
   "cue": "standard"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: initdb builds the data directory, the shared catalogs and three databases.",
   "cap": "Recap: *directory,* *catalogs,* *three* databases.",
   "cue": "shared"
  },
  {
   "say": "Choose locale, encoding and checksums up front. Never run it as root, and replace trust.",
   "cap": "Choose *up* *front.* No *root.* Replace *trust.*",
   "cue": "root"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: starting, stopping, restarting and reloading PostgreSQL. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *start,* *stop,* *reload.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
